                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
          .proof
            %h6#proof_17 Proof
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-cohesive+site"} ∞-cohesive site
              we have that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat} \mathbf{B}G
              is presented by the simplicial presheaf that is constant on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve"} nerve
              of the one-object
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi disc
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G_{disc} \stackrel{\to}{\to} *
                    \\,,
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+group"} discrete group
              underlying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_c
              is however not a fibration.
            %p
              We claim that the canonical inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi disc
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(G_{disc}\stackrel{\to}{\to}) \to \mathbf{\flat} \mathbf{B}G_{c}
              factors the inclusion into
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G_c
              by a weak equivalence followed by a global fibration.
            %p
              To see the weak equivalence, notice that it is objectwise an
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+groupoids"} equivalence of groupoids
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/essentially+surjective+functor"} essentially surjective
              since every flat
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
              is of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mi d
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g d g^{-1}
              for some function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g : \mathbb{R}^n \to G
              (let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi P
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mn 0
                      %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g(x) = P \exp(\int_{0}^x) A
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallel+transport"} parallel transport
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              along any path from the origin to
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+transformation"} gauge transformation
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism"} automorphism
              of the trivial
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+and+faithful+functor"} full and faithful functor
            %p
              Similarly one sees that the map
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi c
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}\mathbf{B}G_c \to \mathbf{B}G
              is a fibration.
            %p
              Finally we need to show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}\mathbf{B}G_c
              is fibrant in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi CartSp
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mrow
                          %mi proj
                          %mo ,
                          %mi loc
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp^{op}, sSet]_{proj,loc}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
              computes
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+bundle"} principal bundle
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
              and then reasoning as above: every
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              is equivalent to a trivial
              = succeed "-principal" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+of+Lie-algebra+valued+forms"} groupoid of Lie-algebra valued forms
          %h3#StrucDeRham de Rham cohomology
          %p
            We discuss the
            %a{:href => "http://nlab.mathforge.org/nlab/show/cohesive+(infinity%2C1)-topos#deRhamCohomology"} intrinsic de Rham cohomology
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Smooth \infty Grpd
          %h4#deRhamCoefficientsInBnU1
            With coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n \mathbb{R}
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)
            be the circle Lie
            = succeed "-group," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#CircleLienGroup"} above
          #OrdinaryDeRham.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_17 Proposition
            %p
              A fibrant representative in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp^{op}, sSet]_{proj,loc}
              of the
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/cohesive+(infinity%2C1)-topos#deRhamCohomology"} de Rham coefficent object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)
              as well as
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^n \mathbb{R}
              is given by the truncated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/de+Rham+complex"} de Rham complex
              of sheaves of abelian groups of
              = succeed "s" do
