              map.
            %p
              To see what this last set is, notice that if we forgot the abelian group structure, and looked at the last hom-set as one of sheaves, we find by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              that is is the set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(U(1))
              of 1-forms. Among these the forms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in \Omega^1(U(1))
              that do respect the group structure are those such that for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in CartSp
              and all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ,
                    %mi g
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f,g : U \to U(1)
              we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi ω
                    %mo +
                    %msup
                      %mi g
                      %mo *
                    %mi ω
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi g
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo *
                    %mi ω
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f^* \omega + g^* \omega = (f \cdot g)^* \omega
                    \\,.
            %p
              A little reflection shows that this is satisfied precisely by the constant forms, i.e. those that are a linear multiple of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\cdots \simeq \mathbb{R}
                    \\,.
            %p
              But
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)
              is not cofibrant in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi CartSp
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mi proj
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp^{op}, sSet]_{proj}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
              and discuss that computing the homs out of that does nevertheless reduce to the above computation.
            %p
              By Dugger’s
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+presheaves#CofibrantReplacement"} construction of cofibrant replacements in the projective model structure
              we have that a cofibrant replacement for a simplciial presheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is given by the diagonal of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+set"} bisimplicial presheaf
              which in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,k)
              has
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi n
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\coprod_{U_n \to U_{n-1} \to \cdots \to U_0 \to A_k} U_n
                    \\,,
            %p
              where the coproduct ranges over all sequences of morphisms of representables
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_i \in CartSp
              into
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_k
            %p
              So we prove now that the computation of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{H}(\mathbf{B}U(1), \mathbf{\flat}_{dR}\mathbf{B}^2 U(1))
              does reduce to the above computation of morphisms out of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 1
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(\mathbf{B}^1 U(1)) \stackrel{\simeq}{\to} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)
              for the above cofibrant replacement.
            %p
              Then a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(\mathbf{B} U(1) \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^2 U(1))
              is a collection of horizontal morphisms in the diagram
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi U
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo →
                                %msub
                                  %mi U
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo →
                                %mi U
                                %mo :
                                %mn 2
                                %mo →
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi cl
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi U
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo →
                                %msub
                                  %mi U
                                  %mn 1
                                %mo →
                                %mi U
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mn 1
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi cl
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %msup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi Δ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi U
                                  %mn 0
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi CartSp
                            %msubsup
                              %mi Ω
                              %mi cl
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\Delta[2] &amp;\to&amp; \coprod_{U_0 \to U_1 \to U:2 \to U(1)} \Omega^2_{cl}(U_0) \times \Omega^1(U_0)\times \Omega^1(U_0)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow \downarrow \downarrow &amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow \downarrow \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta[1] &amp;\to&amp; \coprod_{U_0 \to U_1 \to U(1)} \Omega^2_{cl}(U_0) \times \Omega^1(U_0)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow \downarrow &amp;&amp;
                    \\downarrow \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\Delta[0]
                    \&amp;\to&amp;
                    \\coprod_{U_0 \in CartSp} \Omega^2_{cl}(U_0)
                    }
            %p Explicitly, such a cocycle is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  a collection
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mi λ
                            %mi U
                          %mo ∈
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi cl
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mi U
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi CartSp
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\lambda_{U} \in \Omega^2_{cl}(U) | U \in CartSp\}
              %li
                %p
                  a collection
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi ω
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 1
                            %mo →
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 9
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\omega_{U_0 \to U_1 \to U(1)} \in \Omega^1(U_9)\}
            %p such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : U_0 \to U_1
                  we have
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi f
                            %mo *
                          %mi λ
                          %msub
                            %mi λ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mn 1
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi λ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mn 0
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mi ω
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mn 0
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi f
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mn 1
                              %mo →
                              %mi U
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                          f^* \lambda \lambda_{U_1}  =
                          \\lambda_{U_0} + \omega_{U_0 \stackrel{f}{\to} U_1 \to U(1)}
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 0
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi f
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 2
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ×
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_0 \stackrel{f}{\to} U_1 \to U_2 \to U(1)\times U(1)
                  we have
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi ω
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 1
                            %mo →
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 1
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %msub
                          %mi ω
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 1
                            %mo →
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 2
                            %mo →
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %msub
                                  %mi p
                                  %mn 2
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi ω
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 2
                            %mo →
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ×
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mo ⋅
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\omega_{U_0 \to U_1 \to U(1)\times U(1) \stackrel{p_1}{\to} U(1)}
                        +
                        f^* \omega_{U_1 \to U_2 \to U(1) \times U(1) \stackrel{p_2}{\to} U(1)}
                        \=
                        \\omega_{U_0 \to U_2 \to U(1) \times U(1) \stackrel{\cdot}{\to} U(1)}
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  we have
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ω
                            %mrow
                              %mi U
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi Id
                              %mi U
                              %mo →
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi e
                              %mi U
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_{U \stackrel{Id}{\to} U \to \stackrel{e}{\to} U(1)} = 0
            %p A coboundary between two such cocycles is
            %ul
              %li
                for all
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi CartSp
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in CartSp
                a
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi κ
                        %mi U
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \kappa_U \in \Omega^1(U)
            %p such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi λ
                        %msub
                          %mo ′
                          %mi U
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi λ
                          %mi U
                        %mo +
                        %mi d
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda'_U = \lambda_U + d \kappa_U
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ω
                        %msub
                          %mo ′
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 1
                            %mo →
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi ω
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi f
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 1
                            %mo →
                            %mi U
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi f
                          %mo *
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 1
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi κ
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega'_{U_0 \stackrel{f}{\to} U_1 \to U(1)} = \omega_{U_0 \stackrel{f}{\to} U_1 \to U(1)} + f^* \kappa_{U_1} - \kappa_{U_0}
                  \.
            %p
              We claim that any such cocycle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi λ
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\lambda,\omega)
              is coboundant to one such that
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
                  we have
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi λ
                            %mi U
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_U = 0
              %li
                %p
                  for all
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 0
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi f
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_0 \stackrel{f}{\to} U(1)
                  we have
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi ω
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mn 0
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi f
                              %msub
                                %mi U
                                %mn 1
                              %mover
                                %mo →
                                %mi e
                              %mi U
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mn 1
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_{U_0 \stackrel{f}{\to} U_1 \stackrel{e}{\to} U(1)} = 0
            %p The coboundary establishing this is given by setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi κ
                      %mi U
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %mi U
                        %mo →
                        %mo *
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi e
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\kappa_U := \omega_{U \to * \stackrel{e}{\to} U(1)}
                    \\,.
            %p This follows from the cocycle law for for maps of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 1
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mi f
                            %mo ↗
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ↘
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi U
                              %mn 0
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
