            %p In view of the above gauge condition this is equivalently
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 0
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi f
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 0
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi Id
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 1
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi Id
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega_{U_0 \stackrel{f}{\to} U_1 \to U(1)}
                    \=
                    \\omega_{U_0 \stackrel{Id}{\to} U_0 \to U(1)}
                    \=
                    f^* \omega_{U_1 \stackrel{Id}{\to} U_1 \to U(1)}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This says that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 0
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mi f
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi ω
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi U
                          %mn 0
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega_{U_0 \stackrel{f}{\to} U_1 \to U(1)} =: \omega_{U_0 \to U(1)}
              in fact only depends on the domain of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h : U_0 \to U(1)
              and that as such these forms constitute the components of a morphism of sheaves
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    C^\infty(-,U(1)) \to \Omega^1(-)
                    \\,.
            %p
              But this means that the cocycle
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(\mathbf{B}U(1)) \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)
              indeed factors through
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(\mathbf{B}U(1)) \to \mathbf{B}U(1)
              and therefore the naive computation at the beginning indeed applies and shows that these cocycle are in bijection with multiples of the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maurer-Cartan+form"} Maurer-Cartan form
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mn 2
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H(\mathbf{B}U(1), \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^2 U(1)) =
                    \\mathbb{R}
                    \\,.
            %p
              The same kind of argument as above shows that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \geq 2
              cocycles
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi k
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(\mathbf{B}U(1)) \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR}\mathbf{B}^k U(1)
              have underlying them sheaf morphisms
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mn ∞
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi Ω
                        %mrow
                          %mi k
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C^\infty(-,U(1)) \to \Omega^{k-1}(-)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
              is 1-dimensional. This establishes the theorem for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
              and arbitrary
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            %p
              Finally the same argument that above showed that no nontrivial automorphisms of certain cocycles exist shows the theorem for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k=1
              and arbitrary
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi n
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q(\mathbf{B}^n  U(1)) \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}U(1)
              exist: such are given by a collection of 1-forms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} lamba
                      %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lamba_U \in \Omega^1(U)
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : U_0 \to U_1
              the relation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi f
                        %mo *
                      %msub
                        %mi λ
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{U_0} = f^* \lambda_{U_1}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi λ
                      %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lambda_{U}
              does not vanish for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              for which this is not satisfied.
          %h4#deRhamWithCoefficientsInBOfLieGroup
            With coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            for a Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+group"} Lie group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            for its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
          #LieGroupDeRhamCoefficients.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_20 Proposition
            %p
              The object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}_{dR}\mathbf{B}G \in Smooth \infty Grpd
              has a fibrant presentation in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi smooth
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp_{smooth}^{op}, sSet]_{proj,loc}
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi flat
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}\mathbf{B}G_c = \Omega^1_{flat}(-, \mathfrak{g})
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid+of+Lie-algebra+valued+forms"} flat Lie-algebra valued forms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↦
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi flat
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{\flat}_{dR}\mathbf{B}G_c
                    \:
                    U \mapsto \Omega^1_{flat}(U,\mathfrak{g})
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_21 Proof
            %p
              By a
              %a{:href => "#LieGroupFibrantFlatInclusion"} proposition above
              we have a fibration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi c
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}\mathbf{B}G_c \to \mathbf{B}G_c
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msubsup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi smooth
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp_{smooth}^{op}, sSet]_{proj}
              modeling the canonical inclusion
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                      %mo →
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}\mathbf{B}G \to \mathbf{B}G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-pullback"} (∞,1)-pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{\flat}_{dR}\mathbf{B}G  := * \times_{\mathbf{B}G} \mathbf{\flat} \mathbf{B}G
            %p
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Smooth \infty Grpd
              by the ordinary
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi c
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mi c
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{\flat}_{dR}\mathbf{B}G_c
                    \\simeq * \times_{\mathbf{B}G_c} \mathbf{\flat} \mathbf{B}G_c
            %p
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %msup
                        %mi CartSp
                        %mi op
                      %mo ,
                      %mi sSet
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp^{op}, sSet]
            %p
              The resulting simplicial presheaf is fibrant in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mrow
                        %mi proj
                        %mo ,
                        %mi loc
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp^{op}, sSet]_{proj,loc}
              because it is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_4 Remark
            %p
              Writing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T U
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+Lie+algebroid"} tangent Lie algebroid
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              we may equivalently write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↦
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}G_ : U \mapsto Hom(T U, \mathfrak{g})
                    \\,,
            %p
              where on the right we have the set of morphisms of
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebroid"} Lie algebroid
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↦
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi dgAlg
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi dR
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}G_c :
                    U \mapsto Hom_{dgAlg}(CE(\mathfrak{g}),(\Omega^\bullet(U), d_{dR}))
                    \\,,
          #LieGroupDeRhamCohomology.num_prop
            %h6#corollary_3 Corollary
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SmoothMfd"} SmoothMfd
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow Smooth \infty Grpd
              we find the intrinsic de Rham cohomology set
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi dR
                        %mo ,
                        %mi Smooth
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mn 0
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mo ♭
                      %mi dR
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi flat
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^1_{dR, Smooth}(X, G)
                    \:=
                    \\pi_0 Smooth \infty Grpd(X, \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}G)
                    \\simeq
                    \\Omega^1_{flat}(X, \mathfrak{g})
            %p
              is the set of smooth flat
              = succeed "-valued" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %h4#with_coefficients_in__for__a_strict_2group
            With coefficients in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            a strict 2-group
          %p
            We work out, following the
            %a{:href => "#CoeffsLieAlgForms"} general definition
            the coefficient object for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid+of+Lie+2-algebra+valued+forms"} Lie 2-algabra valued forms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}[G_2\to G_1]
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G_2 \to G_1)
            a Lie
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ξ
                  %mo :
                  %mi CrsdCplx
                  %mo →
                  %mi KanCplx
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Xi : CrsdCplx \to KanCplx
            now denote the inclusion of
            = succeed "es" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+complex"} crossed complex
            = succeed "es/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+complex"} Kan complex
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoid"} ∞-groupoid
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi δ
                        %mo *
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\mathfrak{g}_2 \stackrel{\delta_*}{\to} \mathfrak{g}_1]
            for the corresponding
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+crossed+module"} differential crossed module
            with action
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi α
                    %mo *
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi der
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha_* : \mathfrak{g}_1 \to der(\mathfrak{g}_2)
            corresponding to the Lie
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-group"} strict 2-group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+module"} crossed module
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 2
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mi δ
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (G_2 \stackrel{\delta}{\to} G_1)
            with action
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha : G_1 \to Aut(G_2)
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_21 Proposition
            %p
              The Lie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 2
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi δ
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat} \mathbf{B}[G_2 \stackrel{\delta}{\to} G_1]
              is represented in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp^{op}, sSet]
              by the Lie
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-groupoid"} 2-groupoid
              which on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi CartSp
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \in CartSp
              s the following 2-groupoid:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  An
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
                  is a pair
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi B
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        A \in \Omega^1(U,\mathfrak{g}_1)\,, \;\;\;
                        B \in \Omega^2(U,\mathfrak{g}_2)
                %p such that
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mo *
                        %mi B
                        %mo −
                        %mi d
                        %mi A
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi A
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\delta_* B - d A + [A \wedge A] = 0
                %p and
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi B
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        d B + [A \wedge B] = 0
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  A 1-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism"} morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g,a) : (A,B) \to (A',B')
                  is a pair
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ,
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi Ω
                          %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔤
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        g \in C^\infty(U,G_1)\,,\;\;\; a \in \Omega^1(U,\mathfrak{g}_2)
                %p such that
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                        %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mi A
                        %mi g
                        %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %mi d
                        %mi g
                        %mo +
                        %msup
                          %mi g
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mo *
                        %mi a
                        %mi g
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        A' = g^{-1} A g + g^{-1} d g + g^{-1} \delta_* a g
                %p and
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi B
                        %mo ′
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi g
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                                %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi B
                        %mo +
                        %mi d
                        %mi a
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mo +
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mo *
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ∧
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        B' = \alpha_{g^{-1}}(
                        B + d a + [a \wedge a] + \alpha_*(A \wedge a)
                        )
                        \\,.
                %p The composite of two 1-morphisms
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi a
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi A
                        %mo ″
                        %mo ,
                        %mi B
                        %mo ″
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (A,B) \stackrel{(g_1,a_1)}{\to} (A',B') \stackrel{(g_2,a_2)}{\to}
                        (A'', B'')
                %p is given by the pair
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi g
                          %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 1
                        %mo +
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi α
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi g
                              %mn 2
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo *
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        (g_1 g_2, a_1 + (\alpha_{g_2})_* a_2)
                        \\,.
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-morphism"} 2-morphism
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo :
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi g
                        %mo ′
                        %mo ,
                        %mi a
                        %mo ′
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : (g,a) \to (g', a')
                  is a function
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi f
                        %mo ∈
                        %msup
                          %mi C
                          %mn ∞
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi U
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mn 2
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        f \in C^\infty(U,G_2)
                %p such that
