            %p coincide.
            %p
              Moreover, notice that the lower morphism in our diagram of presheaves indeed factors through the point as indicated, becase for an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E+algebra"} L-∞ algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔤
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
              we have that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g})
              is in degree 0 the ground field algebra algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℝ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi CE
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi vert
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo ×
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} CE(\mathfrak{g}) \to \Omega^\bullet_{vert}(U \times \Delta^0) \simeq C^\infty(U)
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi dgAlg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgAlg
            %p
              Finally, since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [0,1]
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/contractible"} contractible
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/paracompact+manifold"} paracompact manifold
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi([0,1]) \simeq *
              by the
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "#StrucGeometricHomotopy"} above proposition
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Smooth \infty Grpd
              from the identity map to a map that factors through the point.
            %p
              By the
              %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/cohesive+(infinity%2C1)-topos#Homotopy"} propositon about geometric homotopy
              in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
              it follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(\exp(\mathfrak{g})_n) \simeq *
              for all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi
              preserves the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+colimit"} homotopy colimit
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi 𝕃
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi n
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\mathfrak{g}) \simeq \mathbb{L} {\lim_\to}_n \exp(\mathfrak{g})_n
              we have that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Π
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≃
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Pi(\exp(\mathfrak{g})) \simeq *
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_5 Remark
            %p
              We may think of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \exp(\mathfrak{g})
              as the smooth
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-connected"} ∞-simply connected
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+integration"} Lie integration
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔤
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}
            %p
              Notice however that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi exp
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Smooth
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega \exp(\mathfrak{g}) \in Smooth \infty
              in general has nontrivial and interesting
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+homotopy+groups+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} categorical homotopy groups
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+homotopy+groups+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-topos"} geometric homotopy groups
              vanish .
          %h5#for_a_lie_algebra For a Lie algebra
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔤
                  %mo ∈
                  %msub
                    %mi L
