                      \\,,
              %p
                and we find that it lives in the sheaf
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hypercohomology"} hypercohomology
                that models ordinary de Rham cohomology.
            %li
              %p
                Therefore we find that in each
                %em cohomology class
                of curvatures, there is at least one representative which is an ordinary globally defined 2-form. Moreover, the pseudo-connections that map to such a representative are precisely the
                %em genuine
                connections, those for which the
                = succeed "-part" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi a
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_{i j})
          %p So we see that ordinary connections on ordinary circle bundles are a means to model the homotopy pullback
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi H
                            %mi diff
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msubsup
                            %mi H
                            %mi dR
                            %mn 2
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi H
                            %mi dR
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi X
                          %mo ,
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \\mathbf{H}_{diff}(X,\mathbf{B}U(1)) &amp;\to&amp; H_{dR}^2(X)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  \\mathbf{H}(X,\mathbf{B}U(1)) &amp;\to&amp; \mathbf{H}_{dR}(X,\mathbf{B}U(1))
                  }
          %p
            in a 2-step process: first the choice of a pseudo-connection realizes the bottom horizontal morphism as an
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anafunctor"} anafunctor
          %p
            The general version of this story is discussed in detail at
            %a{:href => "#Connections"} differential cohomology in an (∞,1)-topos – Local (pseudo-)connections.
          %h5#CircleBunlePseudoConnection Circle bundles with pseudo-connection
          %p
            In the above discussion of extracting ordinary connections on ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundles"} principal U(1)-bundles
            from the abstract topos-theoretic definition of differential cohomology, we argued that a certain homotopy pullback may be computed by choosing in the Cech-hypercohomology of the complex of sheaves
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo →
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi dR
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Omega^1(-) \stackrel{d_{dR}}{\to} \Omega^2_{cl}(-))
            over a manifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            those cohomology representatives that happen to be represented by globally defined 2-forms on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em pseudo-connections
            over these 2-forms happened to have connected components indexed by
            %em genuine
            connections.
          %p But by the general abstract theory, up to isomorphism the differential cohomology computed this way is guaranteed to be independent of all such choices, which only help us to compute things.
          %p To get a feeling for what is going on, it may therefore be useful to re-tell the analgous story with pseudo-connections that are not genuine connections.
          %p
            By the very fact that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mover
                    %mo ←
                    %mo ≃
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi diff
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}U(1) \stackrel{\simeq}{\leftarrow} \mathbf{B}_{diff}U(1)
            is a weak equivalence, it follows that every pseudo-connection is equivalent to an ordinary connection as cocoycles in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi diff
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [CartSp^{op}, sSet](C(\{U_i\}), \mathbf{B}_{diff}(G))
          %p
            If we choose a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+of+unity"} partition of unity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi C
                    %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\rho_i \in C^\infty(X,\mathbb{R}))
            subordinate to the cover
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mi i
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{U_i \to X\}
          %p
            let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mi ij
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_i g_{ij}, a_{i j})
            be an arbitrary pseudo-connection cocycle. Consider the Cech-hypercohomology coboundary given by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                        %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\sum_{i_0} \rho_{i_0} a_{i_0 i}, 0)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo +
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi ρ
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi i
                        %mn 0
                      %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (A'_i := A_i + \sum_{i_0} \rho_{i_0} a_{i_0 i}, g_{i j}, a'_{i j})
                  \\,,
          %p
            and we can find the new pseudo-components
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a'_{i j}
            by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo =
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mi j
                  %mo −
                  %mi A
                  %msub
                    %mo ′
                    %mi i
                  %mo −
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi dR
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  a'_{i j} = A'_j - A'_i - d_{dR} g_{i j}
                  \\,.
          %p Using the computation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 0
                          %msub
                            %mi ρ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 0
                              %mi i
                          %mo −
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 0
                              %mi j
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 0
                          %msub
                            %mi ρ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 0
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 0
                          %mo +
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 0
                              %mi j
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %munder
                            %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 0
                          %msub
                            %mi ρ
                            %mrow
                              %msub
                                %mi i
                                %mn 0
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi j
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi a
                            %mrow
                              %mi i
                              %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\sum_{i_0} \rho_{i_0} (a_{i_0 i} - a_{i_0 j}
                  \&amp;=
                  \- \sum_{i_0} \rho_{i_0} (a_{i i_0} + a_{i_0 j}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = \sum_{i_0} \rho_{i_0} a_{i j}
                  \\\
                  \&amp; = a_{i j}
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p we find that these indeed vanish.
          %p
            The most drastic example for this is a lift
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \nabla
            of a cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = (g_{i j})
            in
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi B
                            %mi diff
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mrow
                            %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                              %mo ∇
                          %mo ↗
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                          %msub
                            %mi U
                            %mi i
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi g
                        %mtd
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi U
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  \&amp;&amp; \mathbf{B}_{diff} U(1)
                  \\\
                  \&amp; {}^{\mathllap{\nabla}}\nearrow &amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  C(\{U_i\}) &amp;\stackrel{g}{\to}&amp; \mathbf{B}U(1)
                  }
          %p is one which takes all the ordinary curvature forms to vanish identically
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∇
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mi i
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\nabla = (A_i := 0, g_{i j}, a_{i j})
                  \\,.
          %p
            This fixes the pseudo-components to be
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_{i j} = - d g_{i j}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi ρ
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                    %mi d
                    %msub
                      %mi g
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi i
                          %mn 0
                        %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A_i := \sum_{i_0} \rho_{i_0} d g_{i_0 i})
            %a{:href => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle#Properties"} standard formula
            for equipping
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/principal+U%281%29-bundles"} principal U(1)-bundles
            with Cech cocycle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi g
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g_{i j})
            with a connection.
          %h5#U1GroupoidBundle Circle 0-bundle
          %p
            We saw above that the intrinsic coefficient object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)
            yields ordinary de Rham cohomology in degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \gt 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            we
            %a{:href => "#FlatCircleCohomology"} have
            that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}U(1)
            is given simply by the 0-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/truncated"} truncated
            sheaf of 1-forms,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi CartSp
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega^1(-) : CartSp^{op} \to Set \hookrightarrow sSet
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a paracompact smooth manifold
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msubsup
                    %mi Ω
                    %mi cl
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbf{H}(X, \mathbf{\flat}_{dR}\mathbf{B}U(1)) =
                  \\Omega^1_{cl}(X)
          %p
            instead of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi dR
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^1_{dR}(X)
          %p
            There is a good reason for this discrepancy: for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo ≥
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 1
            the object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)
            is the recipient of the intrinsic curvature characteristic morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi curv
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo −
                          %mn 1
                      %mi U
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  curv_{\mathbf{B}^{n-1} U(1)} : \mathbf{B}^{n-1} U(1) \to
                  \\mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)
                  \\,.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbf{B}^{n-1} U(1)
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycle"} cocycle
            (an
            = succeed "-gerbe" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mo ♭
                    %mi dR
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi n
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbf{B}^{n-1} U(1) \to \mathbf{\flat}_{dR} \mathbf{B}^n U(1)
            is precisely the obstruction to the existence of a flat extension
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mo ♭
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbf{\flat} \mathbf{B}^{n-1} U(1) \to \mathbf{B}^{n-1} U(1)
            for the original cocycle.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
            this is the usual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/curvature"} curvature
            2-form of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+bundle"} line bundle
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
            it is curvature 3-form of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bundle+gerbe"} bundle gerbe
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
            we have that the original cocycle is just a map of spaces
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  f : X \to U(1)
                  \\,.
          %p
            This can be understoody as a cocycle for a
            %em groupoid
            principal bundle, for the 0-truncated groupoid with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U(1)
            as its space of objects. Such a cocycle extends to a flat cocycle precisely if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is
            %em constant
            as a function. The corresponding
            %strong curvature 1-form
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
